        transition_time_scale, " model time steps. For example, a high resident-to-resident value means that a resident individual is expected to remain resident across the next time step."), 
        "These defaults are biologically informed heuristic starting assumptions. They are not universal estimates, are not fitted from the current dataset, and are not direct numerical estimates from the cited papers.", 
        "The time scale matters. A daily transition matrix must have much higher same-state probabilities than a monthly or seasonal matrix. Otherwise, the simulation may imply unrealistic movement among residency states.", 
        paste("Relevant studies include", paste(transition_matrix_citation_table()$citation, 
            collapse = ", "), "."), "Use a default matrix for transparent simulation or initialization, then run sensitivity analyses or replace it with local telemetry, mark-recapture, or robust-design estimates when available."), 
        stringsAsFactors = FALSE)
}
